# Cursor AI Rules for Wali Project
# These rules help Cursor AI maintain project organization

## File Organization Rules

- **NEVER create files in root directory** (except README.md, .env.example, etc.)
- **ALWAYS use proper subdirectories:**
  - Scripts → scripts/
  - Documentation → docs/<category>/
  - Data files → data/
  - Log files → logs/
  - Tests → tests/ or python-services/<service>/tests/

## Before Creating Any File

1. Check if similar file already exists (avoid duplicates)
2. Verify the correct folder exists
3. Follow existing naming conventions in that folder

## Documentation Rules

- New docs go in docs/<category>/ (architecture/, guides/, operations/, security/, development/)
- Use kebab-case: feature-name.md not featureName.md
- Always update docs/README.md when adding new docs
- Include date and status in header

## Code Rules

- Python: Use logging, never print()
- No debug bypass code
- No hardcoded credentials
- Follow existing patterns in same directory
- Add tests for new features

## Security Rules

- Check PRODUCTION_SECURITY_FIXES.md before security changes
- No TODO without TODO-PROD: prefix for production items
- Use secure_auth.py patterns for auth code

## Pre-Completion Checklist

- [ ] No root-level files (unless explicitly allowed)
- [ ] All files in proper folders
- [ ] No duplicates created
- [ ] Tests added
- [ ] Docs updated
- [ ] README indexes updated
